# Saved searches: store the query on show under a name, run it in place and in a new tab, pin
# one to a folder and run it from elsewhere, replace one by re-saving its name, rename one, and
# delete one. The run is unindexed, so a this-PC search is saved and listed but not run — that
# is gsearch's rule too.

tree .
refresh

# --- save what the box holds -----------------------------------------------------------
search report
assert-flattened
dialog saved-search
save-search Reports
assert-saved-search Reports
state

# --- run it in place (a template: wherever the tab is) ----------------------------------
clear-search
assert-not-flattened
run-saved Reports
assert-flattened
assert-count 3
assert-status report
shot saved-sidebar

# --- and in a tab of its own -----------------------------------------------------------
run-saved Reports newtab
assert-tabs 2
assert-flattened
assert-count 3
closetab
assert-tabs 1

# --- pinned: saved inside Documents, run from the root, lands in Documents --------------
clear-search
go Documents
search report
save-search Docs reports folder
up
assert-not-flattened
run-saved Docs reports
assert-path Documents
assert-flattened
assert-count 2

# --- this PC: stored and listed; running it needs an index ------------------------------
save-search Everywhere pc
assert-saved-search Everywhere
saved-searches

# --- re-saving a taken name replaces the row rather than adding one ----------------------
clear-search
search ext:md
save-search reports
saved-searches
run-saved Reports
assert-count 3
assert-row draft.md
assert-no-row notes.txt

# --- rename and delete ------------------------------------------------------------------
rename-saved Reports to Markdown
assert-no-saved-search Reports
assert-saved-search Markdown
remove-saved Markdown
assert-no-saved-search Markdown
remove-saved Docs reports
remove-saved Everywhere
shot saved-sidebar-empty
assert-not-launched
state
